From a15b2b43fecbf36e955576a2d6f6bc7855087615 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:56:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add: switch desktops with a touchpad or touchscreen swipe

TouchpadPreferences.gesture_swipe_fingers names a finger count whose
swipes the compositor keeps rather than forwarding them to the client:
on a touchpad, and as many fingers on a touchscreen, where the touches
made before there were enough fingers are cancelled in the client.
They fire the new gesture_swipe_begin/update/end hooks.

setup_defaults() attaches a desktop switch to them: the desktops lie
side by side, as the desktop slide draws them, and follow the fingers;
lifting them past a quarter of a desktop, or flicking, finishes the
switch, otherwise the view settles back. On a touchscreen the desktops
stay under the fingers.
